ue" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668634} :answer-field/id #uuid "a33e8114-f0c1-575b-a1b8-6d10f2763b3c" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668894}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f51862bd-578b-533f-86e5-e297bb989e9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-36244" :question/problem "To which of the following sets do all the real numbers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The set ${Z}^{-}$ contains all the negative integer numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to ${Z}^{-},$ so ${Z}^{-}$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set $N$ contains all the natural numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to $N,$ so $N$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set $Q$ contains all the rational numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to $Q,$ so $Q$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set ${Q}^{-}$ contains all the negative rational numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to ${Q}^{-},$ so ${Q}^{-}$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec1272ac-b97f-543c-9119-57a28276d1b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467342} {:answer/id #uuid "2a8fbbc2-6cf7-5c87-a48c-b6c83dbbfb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a8fbbc2-6cf7-5c87-a48c-b6c83dbbfb36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467343} :answer-field/id #uuid "702309aa-314a-5409-a395-8651b083b51a" :answer-field/key "$N$ (natu