ext} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a1e7823-4cd9-57ea-a117-d119ccf6cf1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673812} :answer-field/id #uuid "f08a95e2-0f53-5e38-8ae6-c4e832b59fb0" :answer-field/key "$\\mathbb{N}_0$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673837}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2593c5be-bd72-52f6-a3bc-cf9ec6b7efe4" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $6.1$ belong?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none of the sets apply, select \"None of the above\"." :question/worked-solution "The terminating decimal $6.1=\\frac{61}{10}$ is a positive rational number that is not an integer.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}$ contains the positive integers (natural numbers). Therefore, $6.1$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{N}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative rational numbers. Therefore, $6.1$ belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}_0$ contains the nonnegative integers. Therefore, $6.1$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{N}_0$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative real numbers. Therefore, $6.1$ belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{+}$, $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673816 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "181b3fa4-2510-5a2b-8fe8-a0b6a630bd1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673800} {:answer/id #uuid "1afabb88-2d61-5f26-a9bd-7c2091c0ca58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673801} {:answer/id #uuid "55557150-74d8-5363-b671-d2567c74c113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673811} {:answer/id #uuid "8dfc76f6-ae55-5154-ab7f-f139bc69a139" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673822} {:answer/id #uuid "fa6cf636-dfce-5daa-97ce-a6517b7aa99f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "181b3fa4-2510-5a2b-8fe8-a0b6a630bd1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673800} :answer-field/id #uuid "f23578cb-4a78-5d47-9911-99c2966d4ddd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673838}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "779d1976-b41d-58cd-bc38-74c04af91388" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $-\\sqrt{82}$ belong?\n\nI. $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$\n\nII. $\\mathbb{Z}^{-}$\n\nIII. $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{+}$\n\nIV. $\\mathbb{C}$" :question/worked-solution "The radicand $82$ is not a perfect square, so $-\\sqrt{82}$ is a negative irrational number.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$ contains the nonpositive real numbers. Therefore, $-\\sqrt{82}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}^{-}$ contains the negative integers. Therefore, $-\\sqrt{82}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{Z}^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative integers. Therefore, $-\\sqrt{82}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{Z}_0^{+}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{C}$ contains all complex numbers. Therefore, $-\\sqrt{82}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{C}$.\n\nTherefore, select \"I and IV only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a660bc6-ca8d-5325-9648-89d6bb379b79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673795} {:answer/id #uuid "0b60a4b7-938a-59d7-bb6f-5ded76f2e24f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673796}] :