 $\\mathbb{R}$, $\\mathbb{R}^{-}$, $\\mathbb{C}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "406f18bc-7a96-5d3f-b302-44adaf9fcc46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673809} {:answer/id #uuid "9b86db33-780a-52e1-91f7-9e20d1b131c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673825} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ec7953-b42e-5492-bf68-72904873dc96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673828} {:answer/id #uuid "c880d8d7-dafc-5322-8cb9-075b3ab8a9c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673830} {:answer/id #uuid "f86fc9a5-c7ee-5308-8a05-157f8999976c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673839}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b86db33-780a-52e1-91f7-9e20d1b131c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673825} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff25c571-373a-5d81-9a52-75dc6572741e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673842}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "892467a9-d66a-5a07-a0e0-d7499c7cb9a3" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $\\sqrt{0}$ belong?\n\nI. $\\mathbb{Z}^{-}$\n\nII. $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{-}$\n\nIII. $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$\n\nIV. $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that $\\sqrt{0}=0$ is zero.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}^{-}$ contains the negative integers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{Z}^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{-}$ contains the nonpositive rational numbers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}_0^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ contains the negative rational numbers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$ contains the nonnegative real numbers. Therefore, $\\sqrt{0}$ belongs to $\\mathbb{R}_0^{+}$.\n\nTherefore, select \"II and IV only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186673821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a41eb87-6bc1-54f1-a4a9-359f1f24bd86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673794} {:answer/id #uuid "0bdc920f-2384-521b-9f42-04dfdc7cb28e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673797} {:answer/id #uuid "21d7ac92-182d-510f-8159-2b1f685785e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673803} {:answer/id #uuid "2b54c966-674b-51a2-b20f-75e73c4356fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673807} {:answer/id #uuid "d314b18a-036e-56af-97db-4afa8887b0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21d7ac92-182d-510f-8159-2b1f685785e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III and IV only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673803} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc0450a5-bc93-578c-8a8c-aff4af77201d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186673841}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8ae5a9e8-d291-5b9b-b8cc-2b490427b95a" :question/problem "To which of the following sets does the number $0.0000$ belong?\n\nI. $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$\n\nII. $\\mathbb{Q}^{+}$\n\nIII. $\\mathbb{Z}$\n\nIV. $\\mathbb{Q}$" :question/worked-solution "The terminating decimal $0.0000=\\frac{0}{1}$ is zero.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ contains the negative rational numbers. Therefore, $0.0000$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}^{+}$ contains the positive rational numbers. Therefore, $0.0000$ does not belong to $\\mathbb{Q}^{+}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ contains all integers. Therefore, $0.0000$ belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}$ contains all rational numbers. Therefore, $0.0000$ belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}$.\n\nTherefore, select \"III and IV only\"."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Containing a Given Element"}]}
